# Echo React (Vite) Guidelines

## Overview
Echo is a user-pays AI infrastructure SDK. Users pay for their own AI usage. This project uses `@merit-systems/echo-react-sdk` with Vite.

## Project Structure
- `src/main.tsx` — App entry point with EchoProvider
- `src/App.tsx` — Main app component with Echo UI

## EchoProvider Setup
Wrap your app with `EchoProvider` at the root:
```typescript
import { EchoProvider } from '@merit-systems/echo-react-sdk';

createRoot(document.getElementById('root')!).render(
  <StrictMode>
    <EchoProvider config={{ appId: import.meta.env.VITE_ECHO_APP_ID! }}>
      <App />
    </EchoProvider>
  </StrictMode>
);
```

### Key Rules:
- Use `import.meta.env.VITE_ECHO_APP_ID` for Vite environment variables
- `EchoProvider` MUST wrap the entire component tree
- The `config` object requires `appId` at minimum

## Echo UI Components
Use pre-built Echo components:
```typescript
import { EchoTokens } from '@merit-systems/echo-react-sdk';

function App() {
  return (
    <>
      <h1>Welcome to Echo</h1>
      <EchoTokens />
    </>
  );
}
```
- `EchoTokens` provides sign-in, balance display, and top-up functionality
- Import UI components directly from `@merit-systems/echo-react-sdk`

## Environment Variables
- `VITE_ECHO_APP_ID` — App ID from the Echo dashboard
- Prefix with `VITE_` for Vite to expose to client code

## Anti-Patterns (DO NOT)
- ❌ Do NOT use `process.env` — use `import.meta.env` (Vite convention)
- ❌ Do NOT import AI SDKs directly — Echo handles AI provider access
- ❌ Do NOT build custom payment flows — Echo provides built-in top-up
- ❌ Do NOT render Echo components outside of `EchoProvider`
